.TH _printf 3 "November 2025" "Holberton School" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
_printf \- simplified version of the printf function
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int _printf(const char *format, ...);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The _printf function produces output according to a format.
It is a simplified version of the standard library printf function.
.PP
It writes the output to the standard output (stdout).
.PP
Only a limited set of conversion specifiers are supported.
.SH SPECIFIERS
.PP
The following conversion specifiers are handled:

.TP
.B %c
Prints a single character.

.TP
.B %s
Prints a string.

.TP
.B %d
Prints a decimal integer.

.TP
.B %i
Prints an integer.

.TP
.B %%
Prints a percent sign.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
The _printf function returns the number of characters printed.
It returns -1 if an error occurs (such as a NULL format string).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B _printf("Hello %s\n", "world");
Output : Hello world
.SH NOTES
.PP
This implementation does not handle flags, width, precision,
or length modifiers unless otherwise specified.
.SH SEE ALSO
printf(3)
